        "title": "Prayers, cremations, grief, re-birth.",
        "text": "“Prayers, cremations, grief, re-birth” We felt uneasy standing across the Bagmati River while observing various stages of wood fired cremation pryres. We felt like intruders as devotees bid farewell to loved ones. We felt more at ease walking about the ghats, one room temples that often serve as housing for the sadhus. We were told that cremations continue ‘round the clock. The actual temple itself is off limit to all non-Hindus. Yet, there is something very human and fundamental here----we live, we love, we die. But if there really is reincarnation, then just perhaps…",
