        "title": "Kathmandu and around after an Himalayan Trekk",
        "text": "After a very good trekking to the Everest Base Camp what a better experience than getting to know the rich Hindi culture of Nepal in Kathmandu manifested all the way through the beautiful and enigmatic Buddhist gompas and chortens (temples and shrines). Now in the center of the country we could enjoy the old temples, actual monasteries, markets (unbelievable Freak St), towns and cities with Arun, guides in mountains and streets. For a flavoury meal, at the New Orleans Cafe in Thamel one block away from our cozy Mandap Hotel and for a pleasent afternoon, a drink at the Kaiser Garden all in Thamel, the tourist zone. A really recommendable four day visit to Kathmandu.",
